a.c('public_contract_groups','Public contract export groups','TypeScript 5.0 publishes gtl.m01 (graph/declaration/admission/serialization/algebra/C/refinement/diagnostic), gtl.m02 (module/publication/lookup/descriptor), gtl.requirements, abg.requirements, abg.m03 (runtime/admission/catalog/traversal/result/replay/continuation/conformance), abg.transport (transport only), app.m04 (SDK/workspace/catalog/invocation/result/replay/F_H/install) and qualification.m05 (qualification/snapshot/manifest/evidence), plus language-conformance corpus asset.',[g(0,81,95)])
a.q('group_export_addresses',['public_contract_groups'],'Exact group IDs abg.contract.gtl.m01, .gtl.m02, .gtl.requirements, .abg.requirements, .abg.m03, .abg.transport, .app.m04, .qualification.m05 locate @abiogenesis/typescript-tenant exports /gtl/m01, /gtl/m02, /gtl/requirements, /abg/requirements, /abg/m03, /abg/m03/transport, /app/m04, /qualification/m05 respectively. Root export may aggregate but cannot replace addressability. abg.asset.gtl.language-conformance-corpus uses manifest asset locator. abg.contract.abg.executive and /abg/executive are reserved 5.1 observer/tuner candidate identities, neither published nor required in 5.0.',[g(0,81,108)])
a.c('public_function_definition','PublicFunctionDefinition<K>','One closed family owns identity, variants, request/result/refusal, authority/effects, indexed binding, capabilities and adapter coordinates; exports/catalog/schema/SDK/CLI are projections without parallel meaning.',[g(0,97,103)])
a.c('addressable_schema_roster','Mandatory schema, vocabulary and corpus rows','Individually versioned, digested, authority-linked and located identities may share groups/documents but remain distinct; canonical schemas and projections derive from one definition source.',[g(0,118,171)])
a.q('mandatory_schema_identities',['addressable_schema_roster'],'Mandatory abg.schema suffixes are product-toolchain-manifest, public-contract-catalog, public-operation-contract, public-operation-invocation, public-operation-outcome, native-contract-inventory, capability-contract, closed-vocabulary, gtl-graph-function, gtl-module, gtl-c-program, gtl-program-conformance-input, catalog-product-descriptor, catalog-contribution-manifest, resolved-product-lock, workspace-binding, install-manifest, installer-manifest, catalog-admission, host-invocation, runtime-event, runtime-result, runtime-replay, fh-interaction, tenant-conformance-manifest, self-conformance-result, exact-candidate-qualification, consensus-subject, consensus-panel, consensus-reviewer-profile, review-findings, review-rulings, consensus-round-policy, consensus-round-outcome, consensus-result, ticket-consensus-projection, release-snapshot and a5-r1-release-manifest. Mandatory abg.vocabulary suffixes are runtime-event-kind, gtl-program-diagnostic-id, gtl-program-repair-edit-class, review-ruling-kind and consensus-round-outcome; mandatory corpus is abg.asset.gtl.language-conformance-corpus. Independent equivalent native/serialized/operation/catalog schema authoring is unlawful despite distinct public identities.',[g(0,118,171)])
a.q('m03_closed_symbol_roster',['public_contract_groups'],'abg.m03 locates RuntimeEvent, CanonicalRuntimeEvent, RUNTIME_EVENT_KIND_VALUES, GtlProgramDiagnosticId, GTL_PROGRAM_DIAGNOSTIC_ID_VALUES, GTL_PROGRAM_REPAIR_EDIT_CLASS_VALUES, GTL_PROGRAM_DEFAULT_ADMISSIBLE_REPAIRS, admitGtlProgramConformanceInput and typecheckGtlProgram; value arrays are machine-readable closed rosters for unions.',[g(0,110,116)])
a.c('prime_qualification_schema','Prime exact-candidate qualification schema','abg.schema.exact-candidate-qualification locates one authoritative document with addressable ExactCandidateQualification<basis>/<verdict>, QualificationLawBasis, QualificationCoverageCatalog and QualificationVerdictInput definitions.',[g(0,173,181)])
a.q('qualification_schema_subordination',['prime_qualification_schema'],'Basis/verdict are Prime-family projections; law basis, coverage and native F11-result input are subordinate definitions, never independently authored schema identities.',[g(0,173,181)])
a.q('corpus_and_serialization_locators',['addressable_schema_roster'],'Language corpus is one canonical content-addressed JSON Product asset with asset/schema locator, digest and expected diagnostic vocabulary; test-only placement is not publication. Serialization locates admitGraphFunction/serializeGraphFunction, admitModule/serializeModule, admitCProgramSyntax/serializeCProgramCanonical, GtlProgramConformanceInput/admitGtlProgramConformanceInput. Installer rows locate AbgTypescriptInstallerManifest and exact canonical install schema; later equivalent symbols need versioned row and supersession, not broad group membership.',[g(0,183,195)])
a.q('public_operation_identity_roster',['public_function_definition'],'The 5.0 abg.operation identities are workspace.create (target/clean|imported), workspace.open (stable authority/readiness), project.read (catalog/runtime/evidence/replay/gaps/actions), product.verify (artifact/contract), product.resolve (requirements), product.install (target policy), workspace.bind (exact set/lock/roots), catalog.admit (contributions), catalog.view (narrowing allowlist), catalog.apply (noncallable node_type|overlay), run.invoke (invoke|start), run.continue (automatic current intent or distinct new selected action), result.assess (assessment contract), witness.admit (reprice|attest|hygiene-stamp|intake|run-resumed|run-stopped), conformance.evaluate (public gtl_program; self-conformance qualification-bound), product.materialize (context_bootstrap|configuration), release.snapshot (published_rc|tapped_release). Derived count neither defines scope nor replaces outcome scenarios.',[g(1,199,223)])
a.q('reserved_variants_and_hard_break',['public_function_definition'],'Observer-report/drafts/tuning-report project.read and tuning.transition are 5.1, excluded 5.0. interaction.respond select/approve/reject/assess/answer_escalation and response-driven continuation are 5.1; automatic continuation/new-action admission remain required. No response capability follows for direct-invoke root or adapter simulation. Retire non-derived legacy identities/facades/registers/defaults/fallbacks; ergonomic CLI spellings only bind one definition without independent semantics.',[g(1,225,239)])
a.q('operation_row_contract',['public_function_definition'],'Each row locates exact request/result/error-refusal/invocation schemas and native symbols; declares defaults, closed domains, actor, read/write/attestation, admission, terminal/nonterminal, exits and per-variant workspaceBindingRequirement forbidden|exactly_one. No optional binding or missing-field completion from prose/CLI/examples/convention.',[g(1,241,248)])
a.c('invocation_outcome_schema','PublicInvocation and PublicOutcome','One catalogued host-neutral descriptor/outcome family serves all operations under selected definition and owning semantic function.',[g(1,250,267)])
a.r('definition_governs_invocation','governs','public_function_definition','invocation_outcome_schema','Selected definition governs invocation and outcome; owning semantic function constructs outcome, ingress validates/admit/transports only.',[g(1,250,267)],governing=True)
a.q('invocation_indexed_authority',['invocation_outcome_schema'],'Invocation binds exact definition/variant/catalog version/operation/indexed authority; required workspace/product/lock/view; admitted program/function for execution; input/allowlist/capabilities/steering/required actor/result-error schema identities. Prebinding forbids binding, workspace/execution requires exactly one immutable binding. Descriptor contains no worker/continuation/event/traversal/retry/selection/evaluation/closure authority; ingress constructs neither semantics nor outcome truth.',[g(1,255,267)])
a.c('capability_definition_graph','Capability-definition graph','Stable abg.capability.<domain>.<name>@<major> identities derive from one graph binding owner contracts and dependencies; tenant manifests publish realized claims, not vocabulary or support inferred from package presence.',[g(2,271,281),g(2,305,308)])
a.q('mandatory_capability_roster',['capability_definition_graph'],'Mandatory @5 identities are abg.capability.gtl.declare, gtl.admit, gtl.serialize, gtl.typecheck, module.publish, catalog.contribute, catalog.invoke-graph-function, catalog.apply-node-type, catalog.apply-overlay, runtime.execute-seven-term-c, runtime.admit-fp-result, runtime.replay-continuation, operator.public-contract, install.bind-products and qualification.self-conformance. They cover declared GTL/module/catalog/C/F_P/runtime/public-operator/install/self-conformance contracts.',[g(2,271,299)])
a.l('optional_consensus_capability',['capability_definition_graph'],['Publish optional 5.0 abg.capability.graph-function.consensus@5 claim bound to exact function and declared contract; retain identity for dedicated 5.1 qualification.'],['Treat absent Consensus as a mandatory 5.0 capability gap.'],[g(2,279,303)])
a.q('tenant_claim_catalog_binding',['capability_definition_graph'],'Tenant-conformance references only exact catalog-present contract/capability identities and binds catalog ID/version/digest; unknown, duplicate, incompatible, unlocated or digest-mismatched identities are typed gaps.',[g(2,310,314)])
a.q('source_blind_builder_obligation',['public_contract_groups','addressable_schema_roster','public_function_definition','capability_definition_graph'],'Source-blind builders verify manifest/catalog, locate all canonical GTL/Module/product/install/catalog/operation/event/result/replay/F_H/conformance/qualification schemas, exact event/diagnostic vocabularies and corpus, build manifest from catalog IDs, derive SDK/CLI/schema/catalog operations from one family, implement native or serialized adapter without source/tickets/history/tests and run conformance/qualification against same identities. Any bad locator/digest/schema/vocabulary/operation/capability/corpus refuses conformance; no fallback code inspection or prose inference.',[g(3,318,333)])
a.l('static_catalog_scope',['addressable_schema_roster'],['Use immutable manifest section, static exports and schema/corpus assets.'],['Require hosted schema registry/download service, signing authority, multi-language generator or hostile-local tamper system for 5.0.'],[g(4,337,340)])
a.c('qualification_infrastructure','Qualification infrastructure','Active exact-Definition-method verification surface has its own correctness law: transport readiness, failure separation, artifacts, timeout contracts and forensic evidence apply to every product-behavior test.',[g(5,3,8),g(6,14,16)])
a.q('qualification_release_allocation',['qualification_infrastructure'],'Standalone Consensus, mandatory host parity, native human response/resume and dedicated F12/S04 observer/tuner are 5.1 claims. Their deferral does not waive local traversal, truthful blocking, runtime liveness, complete selected F17/S06 outcomes or actual human RC acceptance. Ordinary governance/default-library discriminator follows REQ-P-SCENARIOS-018 within S02/S03/S06, not an extra campaign.',[g(6,18,24)])
a.c('transport_readiness','Agent readiness probe','Ready means accepting a prompt and giving coherent response within bounded timeout, not merely being on PATH.',[g(7,30,34)])
a.q('readiness_skip_policy',['transport_readiness'],'Use cheapest reliable trivial deterministic-response probe without substantive work/significant resources. Failed probe causes diagnostic skip, not failed test, since readiness is environment precondition.',[g(7,30,34)])
a.c('qualification_failure_classes','Diagnosable failure classes','transport_failure, no_output, contract_failure and certification_failure each remain distinguishable from test output alone.',[g(8,40,46)])
a.q('transport_failure_integrity',['qualification_failure_classes'],'Nonzero exit, timeout and crash remain attributable failure with stdout/stderr/process truth, never masked as artifact-quality/empty output or success because bytes exist. Preserved artifact rescues only if ABG deterministically validates it as authoritative for that boundary; mere presence is insufficient.',[g(8,42,46)])
a.c('agent_artifact','Agent-written artifact','Deterministic judge evaluates only artifacts agent wrote through tool surface; missing expected file yields artifact-missing with raw preview/path, never stdout substitution or harness synthesis.',[g(9,52,56)])
a.q('artifact_minimum_output',['agent_artifact'],'Below-minimum-viable placeholder is no_output, not a valid artifact to judge.',[g(9,56)])
a.c('supervision_bounds','Layered supervision bounds','Selected test, command, native actor and caller bounds are explicit, ask-proportional and layer-identified, with no mandated runner or historical default.',[g(10,62,72)])
a.q('timeout_terminal_truth',['supervision_bounds'],'Enclosing supervision allows lower owner to report terminal result and preserve evidence. Deadline/process termination names layer/bound and is not completed test/successful qualification. Transport timeout error names timeout value and agent.',[g(10,67,72)])
